2. **Soft proofing**: If possible, soft proof your image on different devices or use online tools that simulate how your image will look on various screens.
3. **Save for web**: When saving your final image, use settings optimized for web use, which often includes compression and color space adjustments that help maintain consistency across different devices.

Remember, while it's impossible to control how every device will display your image, following these guidelines can help ensure your photo looks professional and consistent across the majority of platforms.

