For companies facing resource constraints, an alternative approach to a lengthy pilot could indeed involve focusing on a representative sample of employees or specific departments. This method, often referred to as a "micro-pilot," can provide valuable insights into the feasibility and potential impacts of a four-day work week on a smaller scale. By selecting a diverse and representative group of participants, organizations can gather data that, while not comprehensive, can still offer meaningful indications of how a broader implementation might fare.

